 ## Retries
 
-A capture that raises `GatewayTimeout` is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all (the initial attempt and up to
-4 retries). Before those retries, larder waits 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds respectively. It stops as soon as an attempt
-succeeds; if the fifth attempt times out, the timeout is raised to the caller.
-
-The pauses add up to 20 seconds, in addition to time spent waiting for gateway responses. This keeps retries from
-all landing in the same brief slowdown during the gateway's Friday peak. In the sandbox replay recorded in
-[issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md), this policy would have recovered 57 of 58 timed-out pantry orders. The added
-confirmation-page wait was accepted to reduce manual captures by the payments volunteers.
+A capture that raises `GatewayTimeout` is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all (the initial attempt and up to
+2 retries), with no pause between attempts. It stops as soon as an attempt succeeds; if the third attempt
+times out, the timeout is raised to the caller. Other exceptions are raised without retrying.
+
+Capture adds no retry pauses to the confirmation-page wait; gateway response times still contribute to it.
+Previously, five attempts with pauses of 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds spread retries across the gateway's Friday peak
+to reduce manual captures. Three immediate attempts restore faster confirmation, at the cost of potentially
+more failed captures during those slowdowns and more manual follow-up for the payments volunteers.
 
